# Glossary — Canonical Terminology

Spec: Glossary
Purpose:
  Define canonical terminology used across all .sdd files.
  Each term has a single canonical definition. Aliases map other
  naming conventions to the canonical term.

  This prevents terminology conflicts where the same concept
  is called different things in different contexts.

Owns: glossary/

## Canonical Terms

### @term.TASK
definition:
    Executable unit of work that can be assigned, tracked, and completed.
aliases:
    task, work-item, job
used_by:
    @concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd
    @tasks/INDEX.sdd
    @plans/INDEX.sdd

### @term.SKILL
definition:
    Reusable method for performing a specific type of work.
aliases:
    skill, capability, tool-function
used_by:
    @skills/INDEX.sdd
    @concepts/INDEX.sdd

### @term.CONCEPT
definition:
    Domain or engineering knowledge unit with a single canonical definition.
aliases:
    concept, domain-concept, knowledge-unit
used_by:
    @concepts/INDEX.sdd
    @skills/INDEX.sdd

### @term.DECISION
definition:
    Accepted project-specific choice with rationale and evidence.
aliases:
    decision, design-decision, policy
used_by:
    @decisions/INDEX.sdd
    @evolution/INDEX.sdd

### @term.REFERENCE
definition:
    External or internal source of information (documentation, links, papers).
aliases:
    reference, source, citation
used_by:
    @references/INDEX.sdd
    @skills/INDEX.sdd

### @term.EVIDENCE
definition:
    Information supporting a claim or decision.
aliases:
    evidence, fact, observation
used_by:
    @decisions/INDEX.sdd

### @term.PROOF
definition:
    Evidence produced by execution (test results, build output, runtime data).
aliases:
    proof, verification-result
used_by:
    @concepts/KNOWLEDGE-MODEL.sdd
    @testing/INDEX.sdd

### @term.ASSUMPTION
definition:
    Unverified belief made when planning or executing.
aliases:
    assumption, guess, hypothesis
used_by:
    @assumptions/INDEX.sdd
    @plans/INDEX.sdd

### @term.UNKNOWN
definition:
    Information that is not known and has not yet been investigated.
aliases:
    unknown, gap, blind-spot
used_by:
    @tasks/UNKNOWN-MANAGEMENT.sdd
    @bootstrap/AI_BOOTSTRAP.sdd

### @term.DISCOVERY
definition:
    New information found during execution that may require replanning.
aliases:
    discovery, finding, insight
used_by:
    @timeline/INDEX.sdd
    @plans/execution-plan.sdd

### @term.PROPOSAL
definition:
    Suggested change to the system that has not yet been approved.
aliases:
    proposal, suggestion, rf
used_by:
    @evolution/proposals/

### @term.REVIEW
definition:
    Evaluation activity where evidence is assessed against standards.
aliases:
    review, audit, inspection
used_by:
    @concepts/review-standards.sdd

### @term.VIOLATION
definition:
    Instance where a rule, constraint, or standard is not met.
aliases:
    violation, non-compliance
used_by:
    @testing/INDEX.sdd
    @evolution/challenges/

### @term.HANDOFF
definition:
    Structured transfer of task state from one agent to another.
aliases:
    handoff, handoff-manifest
used_by:
    @bootstrap/handoff.sdd

### @term.CONTEXT
definition:
    Compiled knowledge package loaded for a specific task or phase.
aliases:
    context, context-package
used_by:
    @system/context/INDEX.sdd
    @bootstrap/AI_BOOTSTRAP.sdd

## Loading Priority

  Mandatory terms (loaded at bootstrap):
    TASK, SKILL, CONCEPT, DECISION, REFERENCE

  Domain terms (loaded on demand):
    All others, triggered by domain resolution

Rules:
  [GLO-01] Every .sdd file SHOULD reference canonical terms instead of inventing new names.
  [GLO-02] When terminology conflict is found, AI MUST consult glossary.
  [GLO-03] New terms SHOULD be added to glossary with aliases.

